From 72c4467083f62e67c1bf028a81df22c4ea994312 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Damien Fleminks <damien@fleminks.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:12:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep kitty graphics on file transports with local
 ghostty

- macos: write client t=t files under the per-user temporary directory;
  ghostty resolves /tmp to /private/tmp and rejects it, so every image
  went inline as base64
- a server-retired transfer (placement moved or surface went inactive
  while a file was in flight) now pauses file transfers for one second
  instead of disabling them until the client reconnects; the client no
  longer disables its side on retirement either
- allow decoded file exports up to 64 MiB so full panes on high-density
  displays can use the file route
- let one image that exceeds the inline budget into the scene when the
  client can take files, instead of dropping it silently
- fingerprint image payloads with foldhash instead of siphash
